# Python Port Plan — Step 06 · The Logger

## Purpose

Port `week1_baseline/ruby/06_the_logger` to Python, producing
`week1_baseline/python/06_the_logger` that is behaviourally equivalent:
same `Boukensha::Logger` (structured JSONL session logging, one file per
run under `.boukensha/sessions/`), same `Agent` instrumentation (every
iteration/prompt/tool-call/tool-result/response/turn-end event logged),
same module-level `Boukensha.quiet!/loud!/quiet?/debug!/debug?/config`
state. No tool-calling behaviour changes in this step — it wraps the
existing loop with an observability layer.

This is the seventh entry in the `docs/plans/python_port/<step>` series
(see [`context.md`](context.md) for the index). `05_agent_loop` is the
direct predecessor (not yet ported at the time of this writing — see
[`05_agent_loop`](05_agent_loop)); this step adds `Boukensha::Logger` and
extends `Agent`/`Config`/`errors.rb`/`PromptBuilder` on top of it.

Confirmed via `diff` against `05_agent_loop`: `registry.rb`, `tool.rb`,
`message.rb`, `tasks/base.rb`, `tasks/player.rb`, `backends/*.rb`,
`client.rb`, `Gemfile`/`.lock` are **byte-identical**. `context.rb` only
changes cosmetically (ivar-alignment whitespace). Everything else listed
below has a real diff.

